<title>NORWAY: Aker Maritime increases loan facility.</title>
<headline>Aker Maritime increases loan facility.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Offshore company Aker Maritime ASA said on Wednesday it had raised its credit loan facility by $30 million to $180 million.</p>
<p>The company said its original loan of $150 million arranged by Christiania Bank og Kreditkasse ASA, Den norske Bank ASA and Royal Bank of Canada was oversubscribed.</p>
<p>Half the additional amount is a guarantee for a loan to Aker Maritime by the Norwegian credit institution Eksportfinans. The other half is a revolving credit facility, the company said.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
